0 @N3085@ NOTE This collection contains records for the following years per borough:
1 CONT Bronx, 1898-1937
1 CONT Brooklyn, 1866-1937
1 CONT Manhattan, 1866-1937
1 CONT Queens, 1905-1937
1 CONT Staten Island, 1898-1937
1 CONT Marriage records are an important genealogical record as they do not only record information about the bride, the groom, and their residence when the marriage occurred, but often contain additional information such as birth dates, birth places, o
1 CONC ccupations, and whether single, widowed, or divorced at the time of the marriage. Often a marriage license will also contain information about the parents of the bride and groom including the parents’ names and birthplaces. Copies of the origina
1 CONC l marriage records in New York City are available for order for a fee from www.nyc.gov/records. Marriages 50 or more years old are classified as public documents and are available to all researchers.
